<SiteLayout title="Evidence provenance" description="Archive identity, reproduction boundaries and correction policy for Ardor Lite's research evidence." type="publication">
<header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Evidence provenance</span><h1>A traceable research record.</h1><p class="lede">Recorded findings retain their source identities, original decisions and limitations. Explanations, synthetic demonstrations and current-source excerpts are distinct from historical research results.</p></header>
<div class="prose"><h2>Evidence collection</h2><p>Six cases, 114 scoped catalog records, 204 claim entries, 18 figure/table/specification pairs, five synthetic examples and four other research directions comprise this collection. Those counts describe coverage; they do not count independent strategies.</p><details><summary>Archive identity and integrity</summary><dl class="record-facts"><dt>Archive observation date</dt><dd>{snapshot.observation_date}</dd><dt>Archived files</dt><dd>{snapshot.file_count}</dd><dt>Archive SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{snapshot.archive_sha256}</code></dd><dt>Manifest SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{snapshot.manifest_sha256}</code></dd></dl><p>The archive observation date identifies this evidence collection. It is separate from study periods, report dates and the capture dates of current-source excerpts.</p></details><h2>Reproduction boundary</h2><p>Archived figures and JSON downloads preserve their original bytes. Tables and optional views display saved values; they do not rerun historical research or derive new returns. Historical-return replication requires the private inputs identified in the <a href="/evidence/">evidence policy</a>.</p><p>Selected source excerpts identify captured implementations. A matching path or hash does not establish which code produced an earlier research run. Each case retains any unresolved historical-version discrepancy.</p><h2>Corrections and later evidence</h2><p>Editorial corrections preserve record URLs and the archived evidence. The <a href="/research/cases/delivery-insider/#delivery-construction-discrepancy">Delivery construction discrepancy</a> distinguishes the archived definition, captured implementation and unresolved June run identity. Later evidence must be identified separately; it cannot silently replace the original record.</p><p><a href="/evidence/">Evidence policy</a> · <a href="/publication/">Rights and attribution</a></p></div>
</SiteLayout>
